emic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "\"My existence is a scandal,\" Oscar Wilde once wrote, summing up in an epigram the effect of his carefully cultivated style of perversity and paradox. Through their celebration of \"art for art's sake\" and all that was considered artificial, unnatural, or obscene, the Decadent writers of the late-nineteenth century sought to free the pleasures of beauty, spirituality, and sexual desire from their more conventional ethical moorings. We will focus on the literature of the period, including works by Charles Baudelaire, Edgar Allan Poe, A. C. Swinburne, and especially Oscar Wilde, and we will also consider related developments in aesthetic philosophy, painting, music, theater, architecture, and design.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS, ALC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 367227, "crseOfferNbr": 6, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3754", "titleShort": "Spoken Word, Hip-Hop Theater", "titleLong": "Spoken Word, Hip-Hop Theater, and the Politics of Performance", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 7844, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "02:40PM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "kj12", "firstName": "Karen", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Jaime"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "faci